[Music]  this morning on the dish the James Beard  Award winner for Best Chef northeast  growing up in New Jersey Karen hakuna  what's never planned on being in the  restaurant industry  it wasn't until her 20s that she tried  her hand in the kitchen and soon dreamed  of opening her own restaurant after  culinary school a year in Italy and work  at top Boston area restaurants  she became executive chef at Boston's  acclaimed Myers &amp; Chang that's where she  created Asian style dishes that won her  the Beard Award and other big honors now  she's moved on to that dream of opening  her own venue Fox and the knife with an  Italian inspired menu in a warm wine bar  setting debuts in Boston's South End  early this year we spoke with her  recently chef Karen Nakata whit's  welcome to the dish thank you so much  that is so cool I have to admit I've  been somewhat mesmerized by this  beautiful cocktail but tell her what's  on the rest of it  so cocktail first the Aperol spritz yes  laughs I got prosper it's one of my  favorite hosts Italy perfect yeah cheers  cheers Cheers  Oh dead silence so today we have a  couple different recipes pork has a lot  breaded pork Milanese a with Honey Crisp  apples and then we have some dishes from  the Myers &amp; Chang at home cookbook that  came out last year so sweet-and-sour  Brussels sprouts Brussels sprouts  agrodolce long beans Amandine smashed  fingerling potatoes with chili jam and  cilantro and a little bit of chocolate  tofu mousse that's what I was right with  first eat dessert first that's what  Joanne Chang always says so I have to  say you you started on this endeavor  late in life  I did most chefs start as children yeah  how did how did you come to Italy you  know I sort of came to the kitchen from  from the front door actually from the  other way around I've worked in  restaurants since I was 17 years old I  was a waitress in a diner in New Jersey  I mean that's really my first my first  restaurant job that's where it all  started and and I  love hospitality I love restaurants in  general I love that we come together and  it feels special when you go out to eat  and you know when I was a kid we didn't  we didn't have a ton of money so if you  if you went out to eat it was a it was a  big deal it's a special occasion and I  love that feeling you talked a little  bit about it but what is it about  cooking that you love so much what is it  that just drew you there I mean I think  it's just you know this exactly this  right making food for somebody sitting  down sharing food and what comes with  the spirit of sitting down together and  and eating food together and making  think something for somebody it's a  little bit of like love on a plate right  your first your first kitchen job ended  up being a kind of a trial by a fire  oh my gosh absolutely when the chef got  violently ill that is correct  it was my I mean it was my first day my  first day and my first job as a line  cook there was a very small restaurant  there were only 10 it's actually called  10 tables only 10 tables and the owner  looked at me and said if I don't take  any walk-ins do you think you could cook  for the reservations that were coming in  she said I'll make you know I'll make  the salads can you work the stove and I  in my head I thought I can't absolutely  I cannot do this I have no idea what the  celery's well I've never worked the line  before I have no idea what I'm doing  but you know I said I like you I can try  we got through it we fed people I'm not  sure how well we fed them if anyone you  know is watching this that was there  that night thank you thank you but yeah  that was that was kind of it and you  know as challenging it was that was kind  of like it was also like the moment  where I was like oh this I guess is the  hem what has this been like getting  ready to open your own place it's really  exciting it's of course stressful I mean  that's the reality of it but it's really  exciting and it's you know not to sound  cheesy but it's it's kind of a dream  come true when I found this space I knew  this is the restaurant that I wanted to  to put there I just felt it's a  neighborhood spot it's on this great  corner in South Boston and I think it  just calls for you know someplace that  you know for lack of a better like  someplace everybody knows your name and  warm and well  coming and for me living in Italy for a  year  that's the spirit of Italian dining  right it's the coming together it's  upper TiVo it's you know the most  important thing next to what's for  dinner is what's for lunch and and that  was that's what this this space said to  me so yeah that's exciting I love it  well we want to congratulate now but if  there is anyone past or present oh gosh  share this meal with who would it be  that's a just so many people I just  actually I just saw Lucinda Williams in  concert choice oh my gosh and I am she's  just one of my favorite artists ever and  if she would play for me I would  absolutely for being here for signing  today to see she did a job for more on  Karen and the dish add to our website at  cBS This Morning Calm

